.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Provides a thin wrapper around System\&.Threading\&.SpinLock to expose a busy‑wait mutual exclusion primitive through the \fBISpinlock<T>\fP interface\&. 

\fBSpinlock\fP is intended for extremely short critical sections where blocking or kernel transitions would introduce unnecessary overhead\&. The lock repeatedly attempts to acquire ownership using atomic operations and does not provide any wait/pulse semantics\&. 
.PP
